1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,199
In nineteen eighty-three, deep beneath a
concrete bunker, an

2
00:00:05,219 --> 00:00:10,203
old man lay strapped to a metal table in
total silence.

3
00:00:10,223 --> 00:00:16,415
Every sensory nerve in his body had been
surgically cut, leaving

4
00:00:16,435 --> 00:00:22,752
him unable to see, hear, smell, taste, or
feel a single thing.

5
00:00:22,772 --> 00:00:27,598
The scientists believed that without the
five physical senses,

6
00:00:27,618 --> 00:00:31,805
human thought could reach the pure
presence of God.

7
00:00:31,825 --> 00:00:35,826
Instead, something else found him in the
dark:

8
00:00:35,846 --> 00:00:40,167
hundreds of dead voices that refused to
leave.

9
00:00:40,187 --> 00:00:44,222
And before his heart stopped forever, he
opened

10
00:00:44,242 --> 00:00:48,497
his blind eyes and delivered one final
message.

11
00:00:48,517 --> 00:00:50,689
Let us go back to the beginning.

12
00:00:50,709 --> 00:00:55,948
In nineteen eighty-three, a team of deeply
religious scientists

13
00:00:55,968 --> 00:00:59,925
gathered at an undisclosed research
facility.

14
00:00:59,945 --> 00:01:06,345
They had theorized that our physical
senses cloud our awareness of eternity,

15
00:01:06,365 --> 00:01:12,579
and without them, a human could actually
contact God by thought alone.

16
00:01:12,599 --> 00:01:16,432
An elderly man who claimed he had nothing
left to

17
00:01:16,452 --> 00:01:20,427
live for was the only test subject to
volunteer.

18
00:01:20,447 --> 00:01:26,516
To purge him of all stimuli, surgeons
performed a complex operation,

19
00:01:26,536 --> 00:01:32,478
severing every sensory nerve connection
leading into his brain.

20
00:01:32,498 --> 00:01:37,099
Although the man retained full muscular
function, he

21
00:01:37,119 --> 00:01:41,674
could no longer see, hear, taste, smell,
or feel.

22
00:01:41,694 --> 00:01:45,380
With no possible way to sense the outside
world,

23
00:01:45,400 --> 00:01:48,942
he was completely alone with his thoughts.

24
00:01:48,962 --> 00:01:52,971
This story is inspired by Gateway of the
Mind,

25
00:01:52,991 --> 00:01:56,631
as published on the Creepypasta Wiki.

26
00:01:56,651 --> 00:02:02,391
Scientists monitored him through one-way
glass as he spoke aloud

27
00:02:02,411 --> 00:02:07,831
in jumbled, slurred sentences that he
could not even hear.

28
00:02:07,851 --> 00:02:12,539
After four days, the man claimed he was
hearing hushed,

29
00:02:12,559 --> 00:02:17,054
unintelligible voices whispering inside
his head.

30
00:02:17,074 --> 00:02:22,116
Assuming it was merely an onset of
psychosis, the researchers

31
00:02:22,136 --> 00:02:25,490
paid little attention to his concerns.

32
00:02:25,510 --> 00:02:29,919
Two days later, the subject began to weep,
crying out

33
00:02:29,939 --> 00:02:34,668
that he could hear his dead wife
conversing with him.

34
00:02:34,688 --> 00:02:38,802
He claimed he could communicate back
through his thoughts,

35
00:02:38,822 --> 00:02:42,615
whispering: [subject]"She is right here
with me."

36
00:02:42,635 --> 00:02:47,661
The scientists were skeptical, until the
man began reciting

37
00:02:47,681 --> 00:02:52,842
the private names and secrets of their own
dead relatives.

38
00:02:52,862 --> 00:02:59,368
He repeated personal truths that only
their deceased spouses and parents could

39
00:02:59,388 --> 00:03:05,979
have known, driving a sizable portion of
the team to abandon the facility.

40
00:03:05,999 --> 00:03:12,137
After a week of conversing with the dead
through his mind, the subject became

41
00:03:12,157 --> 00:03:18,435
intensely distressed, saying the voices
were overwhelming his consciousness.

42
00:03:18,455 --> 00:03:22,787
In every waking moment, he was bombarded
by hundreds

43
00:03:22,807 --> 00:03:26,705
of spirits that refused to leave him
alone.

44
00:03:26,725 --> 00:03:31,320
He frequently threw his body against the
padded walls,

45
00:03:31,340 --> 00:03:35,899
desperately seeking any sensation of
physical pain.

46
00:03:35,919 --> 00:03:39,118
He begged the scientists for heavy
sedatives

47
00:03:39,139 --> 00:03:42,658
so he could escape the voices through
sleep.

48
00:03:42,678 --> 00:03:48,413
This tactic worked for three days, until
violent night terrors began.

49
00:03:48,433 --> 00:03:54,437
The subject repeatedly cried that in his
dreams, the dead were no longer

50
00:03:54,457 --> 00:04:00,112
just voices; he could clearly see and hear
them surrounding him.

51
00:04:00,132 --> 00:04:05,348
Only a day later, he began to scream,
clawing at his useless

52
00:04:05,368 --> 00:04:10,543
eyes in hopes of sensing something in the
physical world.

53
00:04:10,563 --> 00:04:15,181
The hysterical man said the voices were
now deafening and

54
00:04:15,201 --> 00:04:19,651
hostile, speaking of hell and the end of
the world.

55
00:04:19,671 --> 00:04:24,090
For five agonizing hours, he shrieked the
words:

56
00:04:24,110 --> 00:04:27,731
[subject]"No heaven! No forgiveness!"

57
00:04:27,751 --> 00:04:32,621
He continually begged to be killed, but
the remaining scientists

58
00:04:32,641 --> 00:04:36,632
were convinced they were close to touching
God.

59
00:04:36,652 --> 00:04:42,518
After another day, the subject could no
longer form coherent sentences.

60
00:04:42,538 --> 00:04:46,607
Seemingly mad, he began thrashing
violently,

61
00:04:46,627 --> 00:04:49,987
biting at his own flesh in frenzy.

62
00:04:50,007 --> 00:04:54,861
The scientists rushed into the chamber and
strapped him flat

63
00:04:54,881 --> 00:04:59,324
against a metal table so he could not harm
himself.

64
00:04:59,344 --> 00:05:03,605
After hours of being tied down, the
subject abruptly

65
00:05:03,625 --> 00:05:06,788
halted his struggling and screaming.

66
00:05:06,808 --> 00:05:10,456
He stared blankly at the ceiling as
teardrops

67
00:05:10,476 --> 00:05:13,547
silently streaked across his face.

68
00:05:13,567 --> 00:05:19,527
For two whole weeks, he lay motionless and
had to be manually rehydrated

69
00:05:19,547 --> 00:05:24,232
through intravenous fluids due to the
constant crying.

70
00:05:24,252 --> 00:05:30,714
Eventually, he turned his head and,
despite his blindness, made direct,

71
00:05:30,734 --> 00:05:37,333
focused eye contact with a scientist for
the first time in the study.

72
00:05:37,353 --> 00:05:41,188
He whispered his final words: [subject]"I
have

73
00:05:41,208 --> 00:05:44,927
spoken with God, and he has abandoned us."

74
00:05:44,947 --> 00:05:49,108
And in that exact second, his vital signs
stopped

75
00:05:49,128 --> 00:05:52,926
forever, with no apparent cause of death.

76
00:05:52,946 --> 00:05:57,693
Would you have severed every sensory nerve
to hear the voice of God?

